{"name":"Lingerie Blue","hex":"#b4d6e5","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lingerie","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Underwear or nightclothes (typically women's), especially when lacy or designed to be seductive.","Linen goods collectively."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lingerie"},{"term":"blue","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a blue hue.","Depressed, melancholic, sad."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The colour of the clear sky or the deep sea; the colour midway between green and violet in the visible spectrum and one of the primary additive colours.","Anything coloured blue, especially to distinguish it from similar objects differing only in colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blue"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lingerie","blocks":[{"text":"Lingerie is a category of clothing including undergarments, sleepwear, and lightweight robes. The choice of the word is often motivated by an intention to imply that the garments are alluring, fashionable, or both. In a 2015 US survey, 75% of women reported having worn \"sexy lingerie\" in their lifetime. In 2017, a survey found 4% of men had worn male lingerie in their lifetime."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Lingerie.jpg/330px-Lingerie.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lingerie","wikidata":"Q855691"},{"title":"Blue","blocks":[{"text":"Blue is one of the three primary colours in the RGB (additive) colour model, as well as in the RYB colour model. It lies between violet and cyan on the spectrum of visible light. The term blue generally describes colours perceived by humans observing light with a dominant wavelength between approximately 450 and 495 nanometres. The clear daytime sky and the deep sea appear blue because of an optical effect known as Rayleigh scattering. An optical effect called the Tyndall effect explains 